# No Release Builds (Efficiency First)

**User preference (mandatory for all AI agents in this repo): prioritize iteration speed. Do not use release builds unless the user explicitly asks for a release/shipping binary.**

## Forbidden by default

Do **not** run any of the following for normal development, tests, inspect, or verification:

- `cargo build --release`
- `cargo run --release`
- `cargo test --release`
- `cargo build --bin <name> --release`
- `npm run build` / production bundling when only a quick check is needed
- Preferring `src-tauri/target/release/*.exe` when a debug binary exists or can be built faster

## Required defaults

| Task | Use this |
|------|----------|
| Unit / lib tests | `cargo test` (debug profile) |
| Build CLI (`exvs2_json`) | `cargo build --bin exvs2_json` → `src-tauri/target/debug/exvs2_json.exe` |
| Run CLI once | `cargo run --bin exvs2_json -- <args>` (debug; no `--release`) |
| Incremental Rust check after small edits | `cargo test --lib <filter>` or `cargo build --bin <name>` |

## Why

Release optimizes the entire Tauri/Rust dependency graph and routinely takes minutes. Debug rebuilds after a small change are typically seconds to tens of seconds. Agent loops must not block on release.

## Exception

Only use `--release` / production builds when the user **explicitly** requests a release, shipping package, performance benchmark of optimized code, or a release artifact path.

